Part A (exact): integral of f_n over [0, 1]
integral of f_n for n from 1 to 20 equals 1 in every case: True
f_n(1/5) for n from 1 to 8: 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 0, 0, 0
x = 1/5: first n with f_n(x) = 0 is 6; floor(1/x) + 1 is 6; equal: True
x = 1/50: first n with f_n(x) = 0 is 51; floor(1/x) + 1 is 51; equal: True
Part B (exact): contributions n times the length of (1/(n+1), 1/n]
n from 1 to 5: 1/2, 1/3, 1/4, 1/5, 1/6
partial sum to N = 10: 2.019877 (rounded to 6 decimals from the exact value)
partial sum to N = 100: 4.197279 (rounded to 6 decimals from the exact value)
Part C (exact): sum of 1/k for k from 2 to 2^m, against m/2
sum of 1/k for k from 2 to 2^m is at least m/2 for m from 1 to 10: True
